"Step out in faith and walk into your purpose” is a saying my Nini used to tell me when I was younger, which makes this project even more meaningful to me. 

Last spring, I developed this concept while I was uncertain about returning for a bonus year of collegiate gymnastics. As many of you know, I have found great joy and passion for dance in recent years. Suddenly, it hit me hard: my gymnastics days are truly coming to an end, and I have no idea what the future holds. I constantly struggle between what my heart wants and what my mind tells me to do. This video represents my journey from being overwhelmed by my thoughts to taking a step of faith and overcoming self-doubt. Consider this my first step forward following my heart.

This project has been challenging yet so rewarding. I am incredibly excited to have created my first concept video! I want to thank my cousin Loren Campbell for her directing skills and for helping bring this video to life. I also appreciate Walker Ucherek for his beautiful cinematography, Sara Ulias for executing my makeup vision, and Frida Esparza for making the ropes look amazing. I couldn't be more grateful for everyone involved!

